==== [1] SIGCHLD handler + waitpid() loop ====

--- [1] WITHOUT: ./server -p 9090 --no-sigchld ---
  $ ./client -p 9090   x 3 (one after another)
  $ ps -o pid,ppid,stat,rss,cmd --ppid 1832
        PID    PPID STAT   RSS CMD
       1834    1832 Z+       0 [server] <defunct>
       1836    1832 Z+       0 [server] <defunct>
       1838    1832 Z+       0 [server] <defunct>
  children left: 3, zombies (STAT Z): 3
  server log:
    | 16:03:08.666 [server:1832] INFO  robustness: [1] reap OFF | [2] ignore SIGPIPE ON | [3] length limit ON | [4] max clients 32 | [5] pdeathsig ON

--- [1] WITH: ./server -p 9090  ---
  $ ./client -p 9090   x 3 (one after another)
  $ ps -o pid,ppid,stat,rss,cmd --ppid 1840
        PID    PPID STAT   RSS CMD
  children left: 0, zombies (STAT Z): 0
  server log:
    | 16:03:09.056 [server:1840] INFO  robustness: [1] reap ON | [2] ignore SIGPIPE ON | [3] length limit ON | [4] max clients 32 | [5] pdeathsig ON
    | 16:03:09.112 [server:1840] INFO  reaped child 1842: exit 0 (request served) | active=0
    | 16:03:09.120 [server:1840] INFO  reaped child 1844: exit 0 (request served) | active=0
    | 16:03:09.125 [server:1840] INFO  reaped child 1846: exit 0 (request served) | active=0
  [PASS] [1] without: the 3 finished children stay zombies
  [PASS] [1] with: 0 zombies, all 3 children reaped and logged

==== [2] SIGPIPE ignored, EPIPE handled ====

--- [2] WITHOUT: ./server -p 9090 --no-sigpipe ---
  $ ./client -p 9090 --mode abort
    OK seq=1 pid=1850 host=LAPTOP-0F0NVT4H up=0d 00:36:17 load=0.03/0.03/0.00 mem_avail=6.97/7.61 GiB procs=215
    RESULT: got snapshot 1 of 10, closing the connection now
  next ./client after that: exit 0 (the parent keeps serving)
  server log:
    | 16:03:09.498 [server:1850] INFO  127.0.0.1:42176: WATCH 10 200 -> 10 snapshot(s)
    | 16:03:09.900 [server:1848] WARN  reaped child 1850: killed by signal 13 (Broken pipe) | active=0
    | 16:03:10.511 [server:1848] INFO  reaped child 1852: exit 0 (request served) | active=0

--- [2] WITH: ./server -p 9090  ---
  $ ./client -p 9090 --mode abort
    OK seq=1 pid=1855 host=LAPTOP-0F0NVT4H up=0d 00:36:18 load=0.03/0.03/0.00 mem_avail=6.98/7.61 GiB procs=215
    RESULT: got snapshot 1 of 10, closing the connection now
  next ./client after that: exit 0 (the parent keeps serving)
  server log:
    | 16:03:10.782 [server:1855] INFO  127.0.0.1:42190: WATCH 10 200 -> 10 snapshot(s)
    | 16:03:11.184 [server:1855] INFO  127.0.0.1:42190: client left before snapshot 3/10 (Broken pipe) -> stop
    | 16:03:11.185 [server:1853] INFO  reaped child 1855: exit 3 (client left) | active=0
    | 16:03:11.795 [server:1853] INFO  reaped child 1857: exit 0 (request served) | active=0
  [PASS] [2] without: the child is killed by SIGPIPE (signal 13)
  [PASS] [2] with: write() returns EPIPE, the child logs it and exits 3
  [PASS] [2] both: the next client is served

==== [3] request line length limit ====

--- [3] WITHOUT: ./server -p 9090 --no-validate ---
  $ ./client -p 9090 --mode longline   (16 MiB, no newline)
  $ ps -o pid,ppid,stat,rss,cmd --ppid 1858
        PID    PPID STAT   RSS CMD
       1860    1858 S+   17808 ./server -p 9090 --no-validate
    RESULT: sent all 16 MiB without a newline, waiting for the server
    (no reply after 1.5 s: the test ends the client)
  server log:
    | 16:03:12.071 [server:1860] WARN  no newline after 524287 bytes: request buffer grown to 1024 KiB
    | 16:03:12.072 [server:1860] WARN  no newline after 1048575 bytes: request buffer grown to 2048 KiB
    | 16:03:12.073 [server:1860] WARN  no newline after 2097151 bytes: request buffer grown to 4096 KiB
    | 16:03:12.075 [server:1860] WARN  no newline after 4194303 bytes: request buffer grown to 8192 KiB
    | 16:03:12.078 [server:1860] WARN  no newline after 8388607 bytes: request buffer grown to 16384 KiB
    | 16:03:12.084 [server:1860] WARN  no newline after 16777215 bytes: request buffer grown to 32768 KiB
    | 16:03:13.572 [server:1860] INFO  127.0.0.1:42206: left before sending a complete request
    | 16:03:13.572 [server:1858] INFO  reaped child 1860: exit 3 (client left) | active=0

--- [3] WITH: ./server -p 9090  ---
  $ ./client -p 9090 --mode longline   (16 MiB, no newline)
  $ ps -o pid,ppid,stat,rss,cmd --ppid 1862
        PID    PPID STAT   RSS CMD
    RESULT: stopped after sending 2432 KiB of 16 MiB: the server cut us off
    RESULT: server reply after 0.0 s: ERROR request too long
  server log:
    | 16:03:13.939 [server:1864] WARN  127.0.0.1:42222: request longer than 127 bytes -> rejected
    | 16:03:13.941 [server:1862] INFO  reaped child 1864: exit 2 (bad request) | active=0
  [PASS] [3] without: the buffer grows to 32768 KiB, child RSS 17808 KiB
  [PASS] [3] with: rejected after 127 bytes, the child is gone 1.5 s later

==== [4] limit on connected clients ====

