    | 16:03:16.478 [server:1887] WARN  127.0.0.1:52480 rejected: 5 clients connected, limit 5
    | 16:03:16.479 [server:1887] WARN  127.0.0.1:52482 rejected: 5 clients connected, limit 5
    | 16:03:16.479 [server:1887] WARN  127.0.0.1:52502 rejected: 5 clients connected, limit 5
    | 16:03:16.480 [server:1887] WARN  127.0.0.1:52504 rejected: 5 clients connected, limit 5
  [PASS] [4] without: 10 idle clients hold 10 children
  [PASS] [4] with -m 5: 5 children, the other 5 clients told busy

==== [5] children die with the parent (PR_SET_PDEATHSIG) ====

--- [5] WITHOUT: ./server -p 9090 --no-pdeathsig ---
  $ ./client -p 9090 -n 10 -w 300   (10 snapshots in 3 s)
  $ ps -o pid,ppid,stat,rss,cmd --ppid 1903
        PID    PPID STAT   RSS CMD
       1905    1903 S+    1820 ./server -p 9090 --no-pdeathsig
  $ kill -9 1903   (the parent server crashes)
  child 1905 still running: STAT S, PPID 1632 (was 1903) -> orphan
  the client received 10 of 10 snapshots

--- [5] WITH: ./server -p 9090  ---
  $ ./client -p 9090 -n 10 -w 300   (10 snapshots in 3 s)
  $ ps -o pid,ppid,stat,rss,cmd --ppid 1907
        PID    PPID STAT   RSS CMD
       1909    1907 S+    1728 ./server -p 9090
  $ kill -9 1907   (the parent server crashes)
  child 1909 is gone: the kernel sent it SIGTERM when the parent died
  the client received 3 of 10 snapshots
    16:03:20.703 [client:1908] WARN  after 3 reply line(s): the server closed the connection
  [PASS] [5] without: the child outlives the parent as an orphan and sends all 10
  [PASS] [5] with: the child ends with the parent (3 of 10 sent)

